ation  captivate her and convince her that  video games are beautiful works of art  that should be enjoyed by people of all  walks of life from all backgrounds and  of all ages breath of the wild did in a  single play through what i could not do  for years and that's when it all hit me  i was wrong about breath of the wild it  is a great game it's one of the greatest  games i've ever had the honor of playing  actually but let me clarify something i  don't think i was wrong to compare it to  previous zelda games i don't think  anybody was wrong to compare it to  previous zelda games i mean  it does have zelda in the title the  zelda franchise had nearly 20 entries in  it before this game came out it's only  natural for fans of the games from  before breath of the wild to compare the  newest entry in the games to the games  that were already out how can you not  compare something that is a part of an  already established franchise with that  of franchise's name to itself but on the  other hand why can't a franchise expand  and evolve into something newer and  greater it's the same for breath of the  wild on the one hand it is perfectly  natural to compare it to its  predecessors like ocarina of time or  twilight princess and get in all the  nitty-gritty of how dense the world is  per capita with enemies or korok seeds  or whatever but on the other hand once  you get past all that comparison and  really just  [Music]  focus on breath of the wild for breath  of the wild's sake you begin to see why  it's so beautiful you know what my  girlfriend said when i mentioned to her  that i thought breath of the wild's  world was empty she just kind of blinked  and said that she actually felt that it  was so cluttered that she almost found  it overwhelming the story was rich and  deep and she didn't mind that she didn't  play through it because to her she was  still experiencing it in a way by  piecing it together the voice acting in  the cutscenes never failed to captivate  her 